>> title: Mashed Potatoes
>> category: Vegetables & Sides
>> tags: potatoes, butter, side, blue plate, stovetop
>> counters: Diner, Meat and Three
>> aka: mashed potato, mash, whipped potatoes, smashed potatoes, mashers
>> pairs-with: turkey-pan-gravy, pot-roast
>> servings: 6
>> time: 40 min
>> step.1: simmer 20 min, started from cold salted water
>> step.2: drain, dry them in the empty pan 2 min
>> step.3: press through a ricer, fold in the soft butter
>> step.4: loosen with hot milk, season

Simmer @Yukon Gold potatoes{3%lb}(1.4 kg; peeled, in even 2-in chunks) in @cold water{4%qt}(3.8 L) with @kosher salt{2%Tbs}(36 g) ~simmer{20%min}, started from cold so the outsides do not blow out before the middles give.

Drain @&(~1)potatoes{} and return them to the dry pan over low heat ~drain{2%min}, shaking now and then, until the steam stops and the surfaces go chalky.

Rice @&(~1)dried potatoes{} through a #ricer{} and fold @unsalted butter{6%Tbs}(85 g; soft) through them while they are still too hot to touch.

Loosen @&(~1)buttered potatoes{} with @whole milk{3/4%cup}(180 mL; heated) poured in a little at a time, and season with @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp}(9 g) and @white pepper{1/4%tsp}.
